 "caveats": [
  "Counts are the atlas counts served today (pre-1.0 counting engine). The sex model only reads XIST and chrY gene counts, which the 1.0 double-count fix changes by a few percent; re-run on 1.0 counts after the atlas re-run.",
  "8 labelled samples were left out because their served atlas bundle has an empty count matrix (a known atlas defect, re-run pending): GSM6815428, GSM6815430, GSM6815431, GSM6815432, GSM6815433, GSM6815434, GSM6815441, GSM6815442.",
  "5 samples are called the opposite of their GEO sex by every tool (GSM5799927, GSM8062050, GSM8062059, GSM9460209, GSM9460213); they are scored against GEO as recorded, so they lower every tool's accuracy. The earlier validation (docs/cell_annotation.md section 4) found unambiguous XIST/chrY evidence against GEO for three of them, so these are probably metadata errors."
 ]
